<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_channels",
    "When invite-only is set, users cannot join unless they are invited by an operator. In Channel List, invite-only rows show a +i badge; non-members see Request Access... instead of Join and can send a knock request with an optional message."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_lightbulb}>{dgettext("help_channels", "When to use it")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_channels",
    "Use it for a closed group, such as a team, a staff room or a private game table. Every new member needs an operator to say yes first."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_terminal}>{dgettext("help_channels", "Usage")}</.help_h4>
<pre>/mode +i                {dgettext("help_channels", "Enable invite only")}
/mode -i                {dgettext("help_channels", "Disable invite only")}
/invite Alice           {dgettext("help_channels", "Invite Alice to the current channel")}
/knock #channel Hello!  {dgettext("help_channels", "Ask the operators to let you in")}</pre>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_lightbulb}>{dgettext("help_channels", "How it works")}</.help_h4>
<ul>
  <li>
    {dgettext(
      "help_channels",
      "Operators and owners can invite people. Half-operators cannot. The invited person must be online and not already in the channel."
    )}
  </li>
  <li>
    {dgettext(
      "help_channels",
      "An invitation adds the nickname to the channel's invite exceptions. That nickname can then join for as long as the exception exists. An operator can remove it at any time."
    )}
  </li>
  <li>
    {dgettext(
      "help_channels",
      "Anyone else who tries to join is refused with a message that the channel is invite-only."
    )}
  </li>
  <li>
    {dgettext(
      "help_channels",
      "A knock is shown only to operators and owners who are in the channel. You can knock on the same channel once per minute."
    )}
  </li>
</ul>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_tab_general}>{dgettext("help_channels", "Channel Central")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_channels",
    "Operators can also open Channel Central, go to the Modes tab, tick Invite Only and choose Apply Modes."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_rules}>{dgettext("help_channels", "Rules and limits")}</.help_h4>
<ul>
  <li>
    {dgettext("help_channels", "Only channel operators and owners can set or remove this mode.")}
  </li>
  <li>{dgettext("help_channels", "People already in the channel are not removed.")}</li>
  <li>
    {dgettext(
      "help_channels",
      "An invitation does not replace a key or get around a user limit."
    )}
  </li>
  <li>
    {dgettext(
      "help_channels",
      "In a registered channel the mode and the invite exceptions are saved and come back after a restart."
    )}
  </li>
</ul>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_link}>{dgettext("help_channels", "See Also")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  <.help_link topic="cmd-invite">{dgettext("help_channels", "/invite Command")}</.help_link>
  · <.help_link topic="cmd-knock">{dgettext("help_channels", "/knock Command")}</.help_link>
  · <.help_link topic="cmd-list">{dgettext("help_channels", "Channel List")}</.help_link>
  ·
  <.help_link topic="feature-channel-invites">
    {dgettext("help_channels", "Channel Invites")}
  </.help_link>
  ·
  <.help_link topic="feature-invite-exceptions">
    {dgettext("help_channels", "Invite Exceptions")}
  </.help_link>
  · <.help_link topic="mode-nk">{dgettext("help_channels", "No Knock")}</.help_link>
</p>
